==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ashamed}}, {{m|enm|aschamed}}, from {{inh|en|ang|āsċeamod}}, past participle of {{der|en|ang|āsċeamian|t=to be ashamed}}, equivalent to {{confix|en|a|shame|ed}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/əˈʃeɪmd/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-ashamed.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Feeling [[shame]] or [[guilt]].
#* [[w:Horace_Mann|Horace Mann]], Address at Antioch College, 1859
#*: Be '''ashamed''' to die until you have won some victory for humanity.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|embarrassed}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|proud}}

